{% from "macros.njk" import callout, snippet with context %}

{% set design %}
<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="d-usage">Usage</h2>
  <p>Lists are the workhorse content component — mail, contacts, settings,
     files. Flint's list follows the Gmail-2020 spec: fixed-height rows with a
     leading zone (24px icon or 40px avatar), a text block, and a trailing
     meta zone. Rows separate by spacing, not rules.</p>
  <h3>Do use it when</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Content is a <strong>collection of peer items</strong> — messages,
        people, documents, settings.</li>
    <li>Rows repeat the same structure with varying text and metadata.</li>
    <li>You want selectable rows that fit a shell (selected rows take the tint
        fill, like Gmail's mail list).</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Don't use it when</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Items are heterogeneous content blocks — use cards.</li>
    <li>Rows need to expand/collapse (accordions) — not in the library yet.</li>
    <li>You need multi-select checkboxes — planned; the current meta zone holds
        one control, but selection is single via <code>aria-current</code>.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="d-anatomy">Anatomy</h2>
  <div class="docs-anatomy">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 600 220" role="img" aria-label="List row anatomy diagram">
      <!-- row frame (two-line row, 72px) -->
      <rect x="1" y="1" width="598" height="72" rx="0" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#dadce0"/>
      <!-- leading avatar -->
      <circle cx="40" cy="37" r="20" fill="#dadce0"/>
      <rect x="30" y="33" width="20" height="8" rx="4" fill="#9aa0a6"/>
      <!-- text block -->
      <rect x="80" y="20" width="180" height="10" rx="5" fill="#444746"/>
      <rect x="80" y="42" width="240" height="8" rx="4" fill="#9aa0a6"/>
      <!-- meta zone -->
      <rect x="480" y="26" width="14" height="14" rx="2" fill="#dadce0"/>
      <!-- spec keyline marker -->
      <line x1="80" y1="1" x2="80" y2="72" stroke="#1a73e8" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/>
      <!-- dense row below -->
      <rect x="1" y="81" width="598" height="40" fill="#e8f0fe"/>
      <rect x="24" y="93" width="14" height="14" rx="2" fill="#5f6368"/>
      <rect x="56" y="95" width="120" height="9" rx="4.5" fill="#444746"/>
      <rect x="520" y="96" width="40" height="8" rx="4" fill="#9aa0a6"/>
      <!-- callout numbers -->
      <g font-family="system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="700">
        <g><circle cx="40" cy="8" r="11" fill="#1a73e8"/><text x="40" y="12" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">1</text></g>
        <g><circle cx="80" cy="60" r="11" fill="#1a73e8"/><text x="80" y="64" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">2</text></g>
        <g><circle cx="330" cy="8" r="11" fill="#1a73e8"/><text x="330" y="12" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">3</text></g>
        <g><circle cx="500" cy="66" r="11" fill="#1a73e8"/><text x="500" y="70" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">4</text></g>
        <g><circle cx="10" cy="101" r="11" fill="#1a73e8"/><text x="10" y="105" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">5</text></g>
      </g>
    </svg>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Leading zone</strong> — 24px icon or 40px avatar (initials text, or an <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> cropped by <code>object-fit</code>).</li>
      <li><strong>72dp keyline</strong> — the 16px gap after a 40px avatar lands text on the spec keyline automatically.</li>
      <li><strong>Text block</strong> — title and optional sub; both ellipsize (the sub wraps to 2 lines in three-line rows).</li>
      <li><strong>Meta zone</strong> — trailing actions, badges, or secondary text (timestamps). Badges sit inline here.</li>
      <li><strong>Dense variant</strong> — 40/60/76px rows for data-heavy screens.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="d-row-types">Row types</h2>
  <table class="docs-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Row</th><th>Height</th><th>Leading</th><th>Use for</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>fl-list-item</code></td><td>48px</td><td>icon</td><td>Settings, simple rows</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--two-line</code></td><td>72px</td><td>icon or avatar</td><td>Contacts, mail previews</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--three-line</code></td><td>88px</td><td>icon</td><td>Messages with body text</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>fl-list--dense</code></td><td>40/60/76px</td><td>icon preferred</td><td>Data-heavy screens</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>fl-list--dividers</code></td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>Opt-in 1px rules between rows</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Dividers are opt-in because 2020 Google lists separate rows by spacing;
     rules appear between sections, not rows. Selected rows (<code>aria-current="page"</code>)
     take the tint fill with neutral text — unlike nav items, which also take
     the accent.</p>
</section>

<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="d-accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The list is a real <code>&lt;ul class="fl-list"&gt;</code> — screen readers get item counts for free.</li>
    <li><strong>Rows with nested controls:</strong> make the row a plain <code>&lt;li class="fl-list-item"&gt;</code> and put the action in the meta zone — only the control is the target. <strong>Rows that navigate:</strong> make the row itself an <code>&lt;a class="fl-list-item"&gt;</code> — then hover/active/selected all work on the row, and don't nest controls in its meta zone.</li>
    <li>Selected rows carry <code>aria-current="page"</code>; disabled rows carry <code>aria-disabled="true"</code> (pointer events are also suppressed).</li>
    <li>Icons and badges are <code>aria-hidden</code>; icon buttons in the meta zone need specific labels ("More options for Q3 roadmap", not "More").</li>
    <li>Timestamps and counts in the meta zone are visible text — no SR-only duplication needed.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
{% endset %}

